  "content": {
    "title": "What's open, closed on Easter Sunday 2026? Stores, banks and more",
    "text": "Egg hunt participants wait in line to get an easter basket after participating in Huston-Tillotson University's Free Community Easter Egg Hunt, April 16, 2022 in Austin. The egg hunt, divided by age group, featured eggs filled with candy and coins as well as redeemable prize certificates, scholarships and school supplies.Sara Diggins/American-StatesmanEaster Sunday is here. While it's not an official public holiday, many businesses and services will be closed or operate with reduced hours.Whether you need groceries or plan to run errands, here’s what to know before heading out on Easter Sunday.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢When is Easter 2026?Easter falls on the first Sunday after the full moon that occurs on or after the spring equinox. This year, the spring equinox was March 20 and Easter is April 5.What is Easter? What does Easter celebrate?Easter is considered a significant holiday for Christians, commemorating the resurrection of Jesus Christ. According to Christian teachings, Christ was arrested, tried and sentenced to death by crucifixion. Christians believe he died on the cross on Good Friday, was buried in a tomb and rose from the dead three days later on Easter Sunday.Article continues below this adIs Easter a federal holiday?No, Easter is not a federal holiday. It is always observed on a Sunday, when most federal offices are already closed. Christmas Day is the only federal holiday with a religious basis.What is Easter Monday?Easter Monday falls on April 6, 2026, and continues religious observances. It is a public holiday in countries like Canada and the United Kingdom, but not in the United States.Article continues below this adWhich stores are open on Easter Sunday?The following stores are expected to be open, though hours may vary by location: 7-Eleven Academy Sports & Outdoors Barnes & Noble Big Lots CVS Pharmacy Dollar General The Home Depot IKEA Kroger Petco PetSmart Sprouts Farmers Market Trader Joe’s Walgreens Walmart Whole Foods Market Article continues below this adHours may be reduced; check with your local store.Which stores are closed on Easter Sunday?H-E-B stores will be closed on Easter Sunday.Ricardo B. Brazziell/American-StatesmanThese retailers are expected to be closed:Article continues below this ad Aldi Best Buy Costco Dick’s Sporting Goods H-E-B Hobby Lobby HomeGoods JCPenney Kohl’s Lowe’s Macy’s Marshalls Michaels Nordstrom/Nordstrom Rack Office Depot/OfficeMax Sam’s Club Staples Target T.J. Maxx Some locations or services may operate with limited hours.Are banks open on Easter Sunday, Easter Monday?Because Easter falls on a Sunday, most banks will be closed, as they typically are on Sundays. Most will reopen on Easter Monday under normal operations.Article continues below this adCapital One branches and cafes are expected to remain open with normal hours on Easter Sunday.Is mail delivered on Easter Sunday, Easter Monday?Standard mail, including packages, will not be delivered on Easter Sunday.Wolf von Dewitz/Picture Alliance via Getty ImagesThe U.S. Postal Service does not deliver regular mail on Sundays, including Easter Sunday. Priority Mail Express will still be delivered, as it operates year-round.Article continues below this adAll USPS operations will continue as usual on Easter Monday, since it's not a federal holiday.Are UPS and FedEx open on Easter Sunday, Easter Monday?Most UPS and FedEx services will be suspended on Easter Sunday, with no standard pickups or deliveries. Urgent services — including UPS Express Critical and FedEx Custom Critical — will still operate. Some independent locations may open with limited hours.Article continues below this adBoth UPS and FedEx will resume normal operations on Easter Monday.Stories you won't want to miss, handpicked by Statesman editors.April 5, 2026Alexis Simmerman has been a trending reporter for the Austin American-Statesman since January 2024. She is a 2023 graduate of the Missouri School of Journalism and has a Bachelor of Arts in English from the University of Missouri.",
